{
  "name": "Landvoice - Daily Lead Export",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Landvoice - Daily Lead Export\n\n**What it does:** for every client in *Client Credentials*, runs the Apify actor `landvoice-csv-exporter` (logs into Landvoice and exports **today's** leads from Expireds, FSBO and Pre-Foreclosure), saves the files as Google Sheets and writes one row per client to *Run Log*.\n\n**Drive layout**\n```\nRoot folder\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 2026-10-18 - Exports\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 Client Name\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 Client Name - Expireds - 2026-10-18\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 Client Name - FSBO - 2026-10-18\n```\nClient folders are only created when that client has files.\n\n**One-time setup**\n1. Import **Landvoice - Save Account Export** first, then paste its workflow ID (from its URL) into the *Save Account Exports* node.\n2. **Config**: set `rootFolderId` (from the Drive folder URL).\n3. Create an **HTTP Header Auth** credential `Apify API Token` (Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <token>`); select it on *Start Apify Runs*, *Get Run Status* and in the sub-workflow.\n4. Select your **Google Drive OAuth2** credential on the Drive nodes (2 here, 3 in the sub-workflow).\n5. Add a **Run Log** tab with headers: `Run Date | Client Name | Email | Status | Error | Expireds | FSBO | Pre-Foreclosure | Drive Folder | Google Sheets | Apify Run`.\n6. Rename the client-name header in *Client Credentials* to `Client Name` (legacy `9` still works).\n\n**Status values:** `EXPORTED` \u00b7 `NO_ENTRIES` (nothing today) \u00b7 `FAILED` (e.g. `LOGIN_FAILED`) \u00b7 `RUN_<status>` (Apify run broke) \u00b7 `SAVE_FAILED` (Drive step broke).",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 600,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -660,
        -520
      ],
      "id": "fa06fe2d-ae5a-43e1-aba3-d6ff1c4e2351",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Prepare today's run\nDaily at 9:00 AM New York time (EST/EDT handled automatically). Finds or creates `<date> - Exports` in the root folder once, then loads and cleans the client rows.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 2200,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "8bcceb29-203f-482e-81f3-c64d002b51b6",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Run a batch of accounts in parallel\n**Loop Over Items** hands over **5 accounts** at a time (batch size = parallel Apify runs; 5 x 2 GB = 10 GB). All 5 runs start at once, then **Wait** -> **Get Run Status** -> **Check Batch** repeat until every run in the batch has finished (or `maxPolls` is reached). The whole batch moves on together.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 1360,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2180,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "5fc60e45-8a70-4d33-8587-c1da7aae2fb2",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Save files and log\n**Save Account Exports** calls the sub-workflow once per account (one after another, a few seconds each) and gets one log row back per account. **Ensure Log Rows** turns a crashed sub-workflow into a `SAVE_FAILED` row so no account is ever missing from the log.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3560,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "bcfe8f18-6047-487f-a13c-26b378e681fe",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4"
    },
